:: But you're immortal, aren't you? [flag:seed_of_death] {"position":"1400,1100","size":"100,100"}
You could phrase it like that, yes.

*Sadness flits across the creature's face.*

I hope to die at last, even though I don't know if it's possible.

[[Start]]


:: Do you need anything? [if:KillTheBloatetOne] {"position":"1000,1100","size":"100,100"}
*The creature looks surprised.*

Yes, in fact, I need something. It has been a long time since you asked me what I need. Could you, by chance, release me from this eternal life?

[[What, you want me to kill you?]]


:: I've found something [requires:seed_of_death if:KillTheBloatetOne if:seed_of_death] {"position":"1000,1300","size":"100,100"}
*A faint smile crosses the creature's face. It gurgles happily.*


At long last, have you really found a way to grant my wish? I never thought it possible. Countless times we have had the same conversation. Countless times I have begged for death. Are you finally going to grant it to me?

[[Yes]]
[[No]]


:: No [flag:bloatedOneNo] {"position":"900,1500","size":"100,100"}
*Anger and sadness alike pour out as the creature screams in agony.*

Why even find it, then, if you're not going to finish it? I don't want to be alive. I've lived longer than I could ever comprehend. I'm tired of living this eternal life. I can't move, can't sleep; not even death is possible. And now, with it so close before me, I can't even get you to kill me. This existence has been nothing but torture. Reconsider, please, and kill me.

[[Yes]]
[[No->Leave me be]]


:: Leave me be [start if:bloatedOneNo item:health_potion organs:20] {"position":"700,1500","size":"100,100"}
*The creature turns away from you, its bloated body sagging with sorrow.*

Take this and leave me be.


:: Start {"position":"800,900","size":"100,100"}
My, my, you haven't been here in quite a while. How have you been? Ah, what am I asking? You've forgotten, as always.

[[Who are you?]]
[[Do you need anything?]]
[[I've found something]]


:: What is your purpose? {"position":"1200,900","size":"100,100"}
I am a fragment of you, in a way. That is why I'm still alive after essentially fusing with the shell of the tower when I died.

[[You died]]


:: What, you want me to kill you? {"position":"1200,1100","size":"100,100"}
Yes. That would be very kind of you. The countless eternities I've spent here have given me more life than I ever wanted. I can't move from here; I'm stuck for all eternity.

Countless times I've reflected on what led me here, and countless more times I've regretted it. So if you could spare the time, please kill me.

[[But you're immortal, aren't you?]]


:: Who are you? {"position":"1000,900","size":"100,100"}
Me? I'm called "The Bloated One". Fitting, isn't it?

*The creature turns its body to look at itself.*

[[What is your purpose?]]


:: Yes [takes:seed_of_death die] {"position":"1200,1300","size":"100,100"}
*You feed the creature the seed. It gurgles as tears of happiness flow down its bloated body.*

*A memory flashes before your eyes: the person this creature once was, and everything you achieved together.*


:: You died [flag:KillTheBloatetOne] {"position":"1400,800","size":"100,100"}
Yes, quite long ago...

*The creature seems to reminisce about a time long gone and forgotten.*

At your side I fought to climb the tower. As I drew my dying breath, you gave me a fragment of your flesh. Thus I remain here, repaying the gift of eternal life again and again, helping you whenever you die. But lately, you haven't come by much.

*After gurgling the last sentence, the creature looks immeasurably sad.*

[[Start]]
